{"agent_id":"pp3g-Fsyf-research-issue-408-produce-an-inventory-of-all-saved","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:54:37.584846903Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b5dcb5d5-6f09-4023-953d-dbe626c50074","comment_uuid":"f6c518ed-4231-40ea-a209-07866c8b8cdc","author":"pp3g-Fsyf-research-issue-408-produce-an-inventory-of-all-saved","content":"# INVENTORY: Saved Sessions + Handoff Docs for Model-Capability and Failure-Mode Mining\n\n**Issue:** #408 — feeds epic #396 (mine saved sessions for model-capability and failure-mode data)\n**Date:** 2026-08-18\n**Scope:** ASES, tripn-astro, crosslink, 100percentaiart, server, Tools, ASES-backup, Tools-backup, HMS, rock-solid-sites, tripn-instagram-feed\n\n---\n\n## PART 1: FULL INVENTORY TABLE\n\n### (A) Session-Handoff Knowledge Pages — ASES\n\n| # | Source | Location | What it contains | Mining value | What to extract |\n|---|--------|----------|-----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| 1 | Session handoff 2026-08-04-173 | `.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/session-handoff-2026-08-04-173.md` | #173 merge gate — orchestrator git merge gated-by-role fixed end-to-end. Gotchas: CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE NOT set in interactive sessions; plugins load once per process; lock-staleness warnings are noise. | **Med** | Failure modes (CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE resolution, plugin reload semantics) |\n| 2 | Session handoff 2026-08-08-156 | `.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/session-handoff-2026-08-08-156.md` | Workflow-topology design delivered; 18 issues closed. Model discipline gotchas (verify IDs via `opencode models`, never Grok/xAI, hy3 long verdicts 504 → chunked posting). | **High** | Model capability (hy3 504 timeout pattern), failure modes (issue ID shifts under hydration, kickoff cleanup --force kills live agents), model discipline violations (#249 Grok/xAI corrected) |\n| 3 | Session handoff 2026-08-08-hydration | `.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/session-handoff-2026-08-08-hydration.md` | Hydration epic #157 closed. Silent-hang class (3x in r3 lifecycle). | **Med** | Failure modes (silent-hang class of agent stalls) |\n| 4 | Session handoff 2026-08-10-341 | `.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/session-handoff-2026-08-10-341.md` | 10 retrospectives filed. Canonical set restructure. Phase-1 auditor validation (CONDITIONAL PASS, caught AC4 overclaim). | **Med** | Model capability (auditor self-correction), failure modes (crosslink kickoff cleanup is all-or-nothing) |\n| 5 | Session handoff 2026-08-14-350-wave | `.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/session-handoff-2026-08-14-350-wave.md` | Read-only-boundary + cleanup-rescope wave. 15+ issues closed. Audit-stall class (#355), rtk double-prefix breaks auditor git (#357), kickoff registry doesn't track tmux-only launches (#320). | **High** | Failure modes (audit-stall class — auditors freeze before verdict; rtk double-prefix; kickoff registry gap), model capability (nemotron 2/2 Nvidia-502 failures) |\n| 6 | Session handoff 2026-08-14-351 | `.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/session-handoff-2026-08-14-351.md` | Filing executed — 16 staged docs to canonical homes. Auditor PASS. Clock discrepancy (live 2026-08-14 vs crosslink 2026-08-10). | **Low** | Failure modes (clock discrepancy; crosslink session start --notes is stale flag) |\n| 7 | Session handoff 2026-08-15-tools-distribution | `.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/session-handoff-2026-08-15-tools-distribution.md` | Tools distribution architecture (EPIC #382). 7 operator decisions. Two review rounds + synthesis of 7 one-shot reviews (ChatGPT, DeepSeek, Claude Sonnet, Gemini, GLM-5.2, Kimi, Qwen). Free-tier Nemotron: 2/2 Nvidia-502 failures. | **High** | Model capability (7-model review panel comparison, Nemotron failure pattern), failure modes (kickoff worktrees leave unmerged branches if content only in shared state) |\n\n### (B) Session-Handoff Knowledge Pages — tripn-astro\n\n| # | Source | Location | What it contains | Mining value | What to extract |\n|---|--------|----------|-----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| 8 | Session handoff 2026-08-04-closeout | `tripn-astro/.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/session-handoff-2026-08-04-closeout.md` | Beds24 tokens, content updates, Node version upgrades, astro convergence. Gotchas: PLAYWRIGHT MCP BROKEN in env; CF secrets don't auto-rebuild; HEAD requests don't exercise CF Functions. | **Med** | Failure modes (Playwright MCP broken, CF secrets don't trigger rebuild, HEAD vs GET verification) |\n| 9 | Session handoff 2026-08-04 | `tripn-astro/.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/session-handoff-2026-08-04.md` | Nav dropdowns site-wide. DB rollback incident. Bash tool kills backgrounded processes on timeout. | **Med** | Failure modes (bash tool kills backgrounded processes, DB rollback risk) |\n\n### (C) Opencode Session Databases\n\n| # | Source | Location | What it contains | Mining value | What to extract |\n|---|--------|----------|-----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| 10 | opencode.db | `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db` | 698 sessions, 33,920 messages, 141,533 parts. Date range: 2026-06-21 to 2026-08-09. Cost: $261.64 total. 245M input tokens, 8.3M output tokens. 373 child (kickoff) + 325 root sessions. Agents: build (208), builder (198), deepseek-flash (81), general (42), mimo-v2.5 (35), auditor (25), reviewer (23), orchestrator (22), north-mini-code (21), others. | **High** | Both — full session transcripts with model usage, token counts, cost, failure traces |\n| 11 | opencode-fork-pp3g.db | `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode-fork-pp3g.db` | 513 sessions, 16,013 messages, 68,803 parts. Date range: 2026-08-06 to 2026-08-18 (active today). Cost: $25.78 total. 495 root + 18 child sessions. Agents: build (246), builder (188), auditor (35), reviewer (33), orchestrator (9), big-pickle (2). | **High** | Both — full session transcripts; most recent sessions including today's work |\n| 12 | opencode-local.db | `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode-local.db` | 77 sessions. Same schema. Local-mode sessions. | **Med** | Both — smaller corpus but may contain edge-case local-only sessions |\n\n### (D) Historical Claude Code Project Docs — ASES\n\n| # | Source | Location | What it contains | Mining value | What to extract |\n|---|--------|----------|-----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| 13 | AI Orchestration Guide | `docs/methodology/AI Orchestration Guide.md` | Methodology spec for AI coordination: orchestration principles, role assignment, collaboration patterns, review structures, escalation strategies. | **High** | Model capability — the methodology that defines what roles exist and how models should be assigned |\n| 14 | Clean Room Execution Guide | `docs/methodology/Clean Room Execution Guide.md` | Guide for obtaining independent AI analysis in isolation. Used for adversarial reviews, capability evaluation, methodology validation. | **High** | Both — defines the clean-room methodology that generated most of the model-comparison data |\n| 15 | Core System Prompt v1 | `docs/methodology/core-system-prompts/Core System Prompt v1.md` | Original core prompt defining reasoning standards (distinguish observations/inferences/hypotheses/unknowns). | **Med** | Model capability — baseline prompt that all sessions were evaluated against |\n| 16 | Core System Prompt v2 | `docs/methodology/core-system-prompts/Core System Prompt v2.md` | Supersedes v1. Same structure. | **Med** | Model capability — evolved prompt baseline |\n\n### (E) Session-Audit Docs — ASES\n\n| # | Source | Location | What it contains | Mining value | What to extract |\n|---|--------|----------|-----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| 17 | session-audit-plan.md | `docs/research/session-audit-plan.md` | Audit plan for 969 sessions across 7 projects. Risk assessment, batch processing strategy. Top 5 sessions by event count (12,004 events max). | **High** | Both — meta-analysis of what was worth preserving; defines classification methodology |\n| 18 | session-audit-stage2-summary.md | `docs/research/session-audit-stage2-summary.md` | Classification: 838 A (ephemeral, 86.5%), 119 B (productive, 12.3%), 12 C (needs review, 1.2%). By-project breakdown. | **High** | Failure modes (what makes a session ephemeral vs productive), model capability (cost analysis by project) |\n| 19 | session-audit-stage3-summary.md | `docs/research/session-audit-stage3-summary.md` | Cross-reference verdicts: 79 Documented (66.4%), 22 Partial (18.5%), 18 Orphaned (15.1%). Key: no ASES session completely orphaned; cross-contamination in project IDs. | **High** | Failure modes (cross-project contamination, orphaned sessions), model capability (what \"documented\" means for AI work) |\n| 20 | session-audit-stage4-summary.md | `docs/research/session-audit-stage4-summary.md` | Deep audit of 40 sessions (18 orphaned + 22 partial). At-risk accepted losses ($32.12). Dynamic Models plugin recovered from disk. Deletion readiness: 951 safe to delete, 8 at risk. | **Med** | Failure modes (at-risk sessions), recovery (dynamic models plugin recovery from disk) |\n| 21 | ases-session-classification.csv | `docs/research/ases-session-classification.csv` | 320 ASES sessions classified (321 lines including header). | **High** | Both — raw classification data for mining |\n| 22 | other-session-classification.csv | `docs/research/other-session-classification.csv` | 123 non-ASES/non-tripn sessions classified. | **Med** | Both — cross-project classification data |\n| 23 | tripn-session-classification.csv | `docs/research/tripn-session-classification.csv` | 526 tripn-astro sessions classified. | **High** | Both — raw classification data for tripn project |\n| 24 | session-index.csv | `docs/research/session-index.csv` | Full 969-session index with IDs, titles, agents, models, costs, token counts, event counts. | **High** | Both — the master index with model+cost+token data per session |\n| 25 | handoff-failure-analysis.md | `docs/research/handoff-failure-analysis.md` | Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview fresh-session experiment: model reconstructed plausible project model but lacked mechanisms to validate accuracy. Degraded into generation loop (token \"producing\"). Context corruption from unrelated domains (additive manufacturing, WWI essay). | **High** | Failure modes (generation loop, context corruption, cross-domain contamination), model capability (Gemini reconstruction fidelity) |\n| 26 | session-recovery-after-crash.md | `docs/research/session-recovery-after-crash.md` | What survives/lost in VPS crash. AD index state. Crosslink issues survive, AI messages possibly lost. | **Med** | Failure modes (crash survival, AD index state) |\n| 27 | combined-verify-server-retrospective.md | `docs/research/combined-verify-server-retrospective.md` | Combined static verification server retrospective. astro dev HMR fragility, base-path confusion, bash tool kills background processes. | **Med** | Failure modes (HMR fragility, bash background process gotcha) |\n\n### (F) Crosslink Gates / Incident Docs\n\n| # | Source | Location | What it contains | Mining value | What to extract |\n|---|--------|----------|-----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| 28 | server-crash-postmortem.md | `docs/research/crosslink-gates/server-crash-postmortem.md` | VPS crash evidence log (Jul 13 2026). Memory exhaustion from concurrent subagents on 8GB VPS. | **Med** | Failure modes (OOM from concurrent subagents) |\n\n### (G) Retrospectives (filed by session #341)\n\n| # | Source | Location | What it contains | Mining value | What to extract |\n|---|--------|----------|-----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| 29 | Phase 1-5 retrospectives | `docs/research/retrospectives/phases/Phase 1.md` through `Phase 5.md` | Phase historical retrospectives covering the project's evolution. | **Med** | Both — longitudinal view of how AI capabilities were used across phases |\n| 30 | Model-Capability 16-Review Wave | `docs/research/retrospectives/topics/EDASES-topic-Model-Capability-16-Review-Wave.md` | Natural experiment: same brief, 8 models, 2 waves, 16 reviews. Agreement/disagreement data. Model routing matrix evidence. | **High** | Model capability — the richest single source of cross-model comparison data |\n| 31 | Other topic retrospectives (7 files) | `docs/research/retrospectives/topics/EDASES-topic-*.md` | Containers, Git-Based, Harness Evaluation, Memory Research, Methodology Research, UI design, microVMs. | **Low** | Methodology context (minimal direct model/failure data) |\n\n### (H) Model Feedback Registry\n\n| # | Source | Location | What it contains | Mining value | What to extract |\n|---|--------|----------|-----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| 32 | 12 model-feedback docs | `docs/research/registry/model-feedback-*.md` | Per-model feedback: big-pickle, deepseek-v4-flash, gemini-3.1-pro, gpt-5.6-luna, hy3, laguna, ling, mimo-v2.5, nemotron, north-mini-code, template. | **High** | Model capability — structured per-model evidence already gathered |\n\n### (I) Other Repos — No Session-Handoff Pages Found\n\n| # | Source | Location | What it contains | Mining value | What to extract |\n|---|--------|----------|-----------------|--------------|-----------------|\n| 33 | crosslink | `/home/claude-code/projects/crosslink/.crosslink/` | 20+ knowledge pages (no session-handoffs). Contains data-model-overview.md, agent-workflow-patterns.md, etc. | **Low** | Crosslink architecture context only |\n| 34 | 100percentaiart | `/home/claude-code/projects/100percentaiart/.crosslink/` | 5 knowledge pages (no session-handoffs). adversarial-review, agent-orchestration, etc. | **Low** | Minimal session data |\n| 35 | Tools | `/home/claude-code/projects/Tools/.crosslink/` | 3 knowledge pages (no session-handoffs). index, server-memory-management, tooling. | **Low** | Tool catalog context only |\n| 36 | server | `/home/claude-code/projects/server/.crosslink/` | 3 knowledge pages (no session-handoffs). server-memory-management, vps-firewall-rollback. | **Low** | Server incident context only |\n| 37 | ASES-backup | `/home/claude-code/projects/ASES-backup/.crosslink/` | 10 knowledge pages (no session-handoffs). Historical backup of ASES knowledge. | **Low** | Redundant with ASES |\n| 38 | Tools-backup | `/home/claude-code/projects/Tools-backup/.crosslink/` | 2 knowledge pages (no session-handoffs). | **Low** | Redundant with Tools |\n| 39 | HMS | `/home/claude-code/projects/HMS/` | No `.crosslink/` directory. | **N/A** | None |\n\n---\n\n## PART 2: RECOMMENDED MINING ORDER (highest-value first)\n\n### Tier 1 — Direct model-capability and failure-mode evidence (mine first)\n\n1. **opencode.db** (#10) — 698 sessions, $261 cost, full transcripts. The richest raw data source. Contains every model interaction with token/cost/error data. Mine for: model-specific failure traces (timeouts, 504s, generation loops), token efficiency patterns, agent-type performance by model.\n\n2. **opencode-fork-pp3g.db** (#11) — 513 sessions, most recent (active today). Contains the latest model interactions including today's work. Mine for: current-state model performance, recent failure patterns, cross-session behavior.\n\n3. **session-index.csv** (#24) — The master index of all 969 sessions with model, cost, tokens, event counts. Pre-processed and ready for statistical analysis. Start here before diving into raw DB transcripts.\n\n4. **ases-session-classification.csv** (#21) + **tripn-session-classification.csv** (#23) + **other-session-classification.csv** (#22) — Pre-classified session data (A/B/C categories). Already cross-referenced with git and crosslink.\n\n5. **EDASES-topic-Model-Capability-16-Review-Wave.md** (#30) — The richest single analysis document: 8 models, 2 waves, 16 reviews, agreement matrices, synthesis. Already synthesized but needs extraction into failure matrix and capability registry formats.\n\n6. **Model-feedback registry** (#32) — 12 structured per-model feedback docs. Ready for direct extraction into capability registry (#255/#346) and failure matrix (#407).\n\n### Tier 2 — Session handoffs with high failure-mode content (mine second)\n\n7. **session-handoff-2026-08-15-tools-distribution** (#7) — 7-model review panel + Nemotron failure data.\n8. **session-handoff-2026-08-08-156** (#2) — Model discipline violations, hy3 504 pattern, issue ID shift gotcha.\n9. **session-handoff-2026-08-14-350-wave** (#5) — Audit-stall class, rtk double-prefix, Nemotron failures.\n\n### Tier 3 — Audit/meta-analysis docs (mine third)\n\n10. **session-audit-stage2-summary.md** (#18) — Classification methodology + what makes sessions ephemeral.\n11. **session-audit-stage3-summary.md** (#19) — Orphaned session patterns, cross-project contamination.\n12. **handoff-failure-analysis.md** (#25) — Gemini 3.1 Pro fresh-session reconstruction failure (generation loop, context corruption).\n13. **session-audit-plan.md** (#17) — Meta-analysis of 969 sessions.\n\n### Tier 4 — Methodology + historical context (mine fourth)\n\n14. **AI Orchestration Guide** (#13) — Defines the role/model assignment methodology.\n15. **Clean Room Execution Guide** (#14) — Defines the isolation methodology that generated comparison data.\n16. **Core System Prompts v1/v2** (#15, #16) — Baseline prompts used across sessions.\n\n### Tier 5 — Supplementary handoffs + incident docs (mine last)\n\n17. Remaining 6 ASES handoff pages (#1, #3, #4, #6) + 2 tripn-astro handoffs (#8, #9).\n18. **session-recovery-after-crash.md** (#26) + **server-crash-postmortem.md** (#28) + **combined-verify-server-retrospective.md** (#27).\n19. **opencode-local.db** (#12) — 77 sessions, smaller but may contain edge cases.\n\n---\n\n## PART 3: OPENCODE DB NOTES — Interactive vs Agent-Tmux Session Distinction\n\n### Schema fields that distinguish session types\n\n| Field | How to identify | Notes |\n|-------|----------------|-------|\n| `parent_id` | NULL = root (interactive or first-session); non-NULL = child (kickoff sub-agent) | opencode.db: 325 root + 373 child; fork DB: 495 root + 18 child |\n| `agent` | Values: build, builder, orchestrator, auditor, reviewer, general, etc. | \"build\"/\"builder\" = kickoffs; \"orchestrator\"/\"auditor\"/\"reviewer\" = swarm roles; \"general\"/\"deepseek-flash\"/\"mimo-v2.5\" = interactive sessions using named agents |\n| `workspace_id` | Links to workspace table — identifies which worktree | NULL = main repo sessions; non-NULL = worktree sessions |\n| `directory` | Full path to working directory | Contains \".worktrees/\" for isolated feature work |\n\n### Recommended pruning approach\n\n1. **NEVER prune interactive sessions** — these are the operator's personal sessions containing human reasoning and decisions. Identify by: `parent_id IS NULL AND agent IN ('general', 'deepseek-flash', 'mimo-v2.5', 'mimo-general', 'laguna-general')` or agent IS NULL.\n\n2. **Prune agent-tmux sessions that are fully documented** — child sessions where: (a) the corresponding crosslink issue has a --kind result comment, AND (b) the session's work is in git commits. Query: `SELECT s.id, s.title, s.agent FROM session s WHERE s.parent_id IS NOT NULL` then cross-reference with crosslink issues.\n\n3. **Preserve agent-tmux sessions that are NOT documented** — the stage3 audit found 18 orphaned sessions; some may still be in the DB. These are candidates for mining, not pruning.\n\n4. **Compact before deleting** — opencode's `--compact` removes tool output (part table) while keeping session metadata and messages. Run `opencode session compact <id>` for sessions to be preserved but not actively mined.\n\n5. **Export before deleting** — for any session with model-capability data (unusual model, failure trace, long conversation), export the messages table first: `sqlite3 opencode.db \"SELECT * FROM session_message WHERE session_id = '...'\" > /tmp/export.json`\n\n6. **Size budget**: opencode.db = 2.47 GB, fork DB = 2.58 GB, total = 5.05 GB. Tool output = 1 MB. The bulk is in messages/parts tables. After compacting all documented sessions, expect ~60-70% reduction.\n\n### Interactive sessions worth preserving (by model)\n\nThe opencode.db contains sessions for these models that may have unique capability data:\n- `deepseek-flash` (81 sessions) — free-tier model behavior patterns\n- `mimo-v2.5` (35 sessions) — paid model baseline\n- `north-mini-code` (21 sessions) — specialized agent behavior\n- `gemini-35-flash` (4 sessions) — cross-provider comparison\n- `hy3` (2 sessions) — known 504 timeout pattern\n\n---\n\n## PART 4: FAILURE MATRIX (#407) vs AI CAPABILITY REGISTRY (#255/#346) ROUTING\n\n### Entries that feed the FAILURE MATRIX (#407)\n\n| Entry | What to extract |\n|-------|-----------------|\n| opencode.db (#10) + fork DB (#11) | Error traces, timeout patterns, generation loops, crash signatures per model |\n| session-audit-stage2 (#18) | What makes a session ephemeral (failure class) |\n| session-audit-stage3 (#19) | Orphaned session patterns, cross-project contamination |\n| session-audit-stage4 (#20) | At-risk session categories, deletion-safe vs loss-risk |\n| handoff-failure-analysis (#25) | Generation loop (Gemini), context corruption, cross-domain contamination |\n| session-recovery-after-crash (#26) | Crash survival/failure modes, AD index state |\n| server-crash-postmortem (#28) | OOM from concurrent subagents |\n| session-handoff-2026-08-08-hydration (#3) | Silent-hang class (3x in lifecycle) |\n| session-handoff-2026-08-14-350-wave (#5) | Audit-stall class, rtk double-prefix, kickoff registry gap |\n| session-handoff-2026-08-04-173 (#1) | CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE not set, plugin load-once |\n| session-handoff-2026-08-04-closeout (#8) | Playwright MCP broken, CF secrets don't rebuild |\n| session-handoff-2026-08-04 (#9) | Bash kills backgrounded processes, DB rollback risk |\n| session-handoff-2026-08-15-tools-distribution (#7) | Nemotron 2/2 Nvidia-502 failures |\n| combined-verify-server-retrospective (#27) | HMR fragility, bash background gotcha |\n| session-index.csv (#24) | Statistical failure patterns (cost outliers, zero-event sessions) |\n\n### Entries that feed the AI CAPABILITY REGISTRY (#255/#346)\n\n| Entry | What to extract |\n|-------|-----------------|\n| Model-Capability 16-Review Wave (#30) | Cross-model agreement data, synthesis findings, routing evidence |\n| Model-feedback registry (#32, 12 docs) | Per-model structured evidence (already in registry-ready format) |\n| session-handoff-2026-08-15-tools-distribution (#7) | 7-model review panel comparison |\n| session-handoff-2026-08-08-156 (#2) | Model discipline evidence (what models can/can't do) |\n| AI Orchestration Guide (#13) | Role definitions that models are assigned to |\n| Clean Room Execution Guide (#14) | Isolation methodology for capability measurement |\n| Core System Prompts (#15, #16) | Prompt baselines for evaluation |\n| opencode.db (#10) + fork DB (#11) | Token efficiency, cost-per-task, model availability data |\n| session-index.csv (#24) | Model cost/token aggregates |\n| ases/tripn/other classification CSVs (#21-23) | Per-project model usage patterns |\n| Phase retrospectives (#29) | Longitudinal capability evolution |\n\n### Entries that feed BOTH\n\n| Entry | Why both |\n|-------|----------|\n| opencode.db (#10) + fork DB (#11) | Contains both failure traces AND capability evidence in raw transcripts |\n| session-index.csv (#24) | Failure patterns (anomalies) AND capability patterns (cost/token efficiency) |\n| Classification CSVs (#21-23) | Ephemeral = failure class; productive = capability evidence |\n| session-handoff-2026-08-14-350-wave (#5) | Audit-stall = failure; Nemotron failures = capability |\n| session-handoff-2026-08-08-156 (#2) | Issue ID shift = failure; model discipline = capability |","created_at":"2026-08-18T14:54:37.574407419Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:EvHn2u3uGRe+YZGnIF5PjVL6rKgcGF7Ku/8rCSvuesc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDBP8scjb7po5PyE8paif3Px+5s2OJsJ4O0y6rDG5InEAAAA